            <ArticleTitle>Ethical Issues with Genetic Testing for Tay-Sachs.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>246-249</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1097/CNJ.0000000000000426</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Several genetic disorders are specific to Jewish heritage; one of the most devastating is Tay-Sachs disease.Tay-Sachs is a fatal hereditary disease, causing progressive neurological problems for which there is no cure. Ethical issues surrounding genetic testing for Tay-Sachs within the Jewish community continue to be complex and multifaceted. A perspective of Tay-Sachs, using rights-based ethics and virtue ethics as a theoretical framework, is explored.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
